Description: Wild OS Backup
 Backup keeps encrypted copies of your files on your own external drive,
 with restic. Every day at a time you choose it backs up your home
 folder, Mail, Calendar, People and Tasks, and your app settings, and
 catches up when the drive is plugged back in after a missed backup.
 Old backups are thinned out over a year, oldest first when the drive is
 nearly full. Browse any backup by date and put files back where they
 were, or anywhere you like. Windows mode's disk can be backed up too,
 while Windows is shut down. The password is made for you and kept in
 your keyring. Nothing leaves the PC: no cloud and no network.
